# AI Tools

These tools provide narrow Unreal AI authoring probes and smoke tests for the
UE 5.6.1 MCP bridge. They are authoring/verification helpers only: generated
or tested content must remain standard engine/project content and must not
serialize references to UnrealMCP.

## Tools

- `inspect_ai_authoring_support()`
  - Checks which AI classes are exposed to Unreal Python in the running editor.
  - Reports support for `AIController`, `AIPerceptionComponent`,
    `BehaviorTree`, `BlackboardData`, and related factories.
- `run_ai_dummy_patrol_chase_smoke(...)`
  - Builds a temporary current-level fixture using the Cubeless Piper character
    by default.
  - Starts SIE, commands an `AIController` to patrol, moves a player dummy into
    sight range, checks `AIController.line_of_sight_to`, then commands the AI to
    follow the player.
  - Writes numeric evidence under `Docs/Analysis/AIDummySmoke/` by default.
- `create_ai_patrol_chase_behavior_assets(...)`
  - Uses the editor-only C++ helper
    `create_ai_patrol_chase_behavior_assets` to create standard Unreal
    `UBehaviorTree` and `UBlackboardData` assets.
  - Creates a standard Blackboard with `TargetActor` as an Object key,
    `PatrolLocation` and `LastKnownTargetLocation` as Vector keys, and
    `AIState` as a Name key. Engine readback can also include the standard
    `SelfActor` key.
  - `tree_shape="sequence_patrol_chase"` creates the original simple root
    sequence: patrol location, then target actor.
  - `tree_shape="selector_chase_patrol"` creates a root selector that tries
    `TargetActor` first, then falls back to `PatrolLocation` when the target
    key is unset.
  - `tree_shape="selector_alert_chase_patrol"` creates a root selector with a
    `FaceThenChaseTarget` sequence (`UBTTask_RotateToFaceBBEntry`,
    `UBTTask_Wait`, `UBTTask_MoveDirectlyToward`) before falling back to
    patrol movement.
  - Selector shapes add a standard `UBTDecorator_Blackboard` to the chase
    branch. It checks `TargetActor` is set and uses `Both` flow aborts so the
    tree reacts when a target appears or changes while patrol is running.
  - Movement shapes use standard `UBTTask_MoveDirectlyToward` children. The
    direct task keeps smoke tests reliable in temporary no-NavMesh levels while
    staying on stock `AIModule` classes.
  - Defaults to `save_assets=false` so smoke checks do not write `.uasset`
    files unless explicitly requested.
  - `replace_existing=true` deletes and recreates the existing Behavior Tree
    and Blackboard pair. Search dispatch therefore requires explicit
    confirmation for that mode; keep a source-control restore point or backup.
- `configure_ai_controller_perception(...)`
  - Uses the editor-only C++ helper `configure_ai_controller_perception` to add
    or find a standard `UAIPerceptionComponent` on an AIController Blueprint.
  - Configures `UAISenseConfig_Sight`, dominant `UAISense_Sight`, sight radius,
    lose-sight radius, peripheral vision angle, stimulus max age, and
    affiliation detection.
  - Exists because Unreal Python exposes the classes but not the stable
    `ConfigureSense` / `SetDominantSense` calls needed to persist a reliable
    perception setup.
- `inspect_ai_behavior_assets(...)`
  - Reloads saved BT/BB assets through the C++ helper and reports root node,
    child tasks, Blackboard keys, editor graph presence, and MCP dependency
    audit status.
- `run_ai_behavior_tree_execution_smoke(...)`
  - Starts SIE, loads the saved BT/BB assets, calls
    `AIController.use_blackboard` and `AIController.run_behavior_tree`, writes
    `TargetActor` and `PatrolLocation`, then verifies movement evidence.

### UE 5.6 AI asset authoring

This surface is intentionally specialized for Unreal Engine 5.6.1. It uses
only APIs verified in the local UE 5.6 engine source and does not carry UE 5.7
or UE 5.8 compatibility branches.

- `list_ai_assets(asset_root="/Game", asset_type="all", ...)`
  - Uses Unreal Python and the Asset Registry to list standard `BehaviorTree`,
    `BlackboardData`, and `EnvQuery` assets.
  - `asset_type` accepts `all`, `behavior_tree`, `blackboard`, or `eqs`.
- `inspect_ai_asset_structure(asset_path, ...)`
  - Reads a single Behavior Tree, Blackboard, or EQS asset through the native
    UE 5.6 helper.
  - Behavior Trees report runtime hierarchy, decorators, services, linked
    Blackboard, and editor graph state. Blackboards separate own and inherited
    typed keys. EQS assets report option and editor-graph counts.
- `create_ai_blackboard_asset(asset_name, asset_root="/Game/AI", ...)`
  - Creates and saves an empty standard `UBlackboardData` asset.
  - Existing assets are never replaced.
- `add_ai_blackboard_key(blackboard_path, key_name, key_type, ...)`
  - Adds one UE 5.6 Blackboard key of type `bool`, `class`, `enum`, `float`,
    `int`, `name`, `object`, `rotator`, `string`, or `vector`.
  - Object/Class keys accept an exact `base_class` object path. Enum keys
    require `enum_path` and reject values outside the Blackboard byte range.
  - Inherited and engine-provided keys cannot be shadowed.
- `remove_ai_blackboard_key(blackboard_path, key_name, ...)`
  - Removes one locally owned key. Inherited and engine-provided keys are
    rejected.
  - The operation does not rewrite Behavior Tree nodes that referenced the
    removed key; inspect dependent trees before removal.
- `create_ai_behavior_tree_asset(asset_name, asset_root="/Game/AI", ...)`
  - Creates a standard `UBehaviorTree` and its UE 5.6 editor graph, optionally
    linked to an existing Blackboard.
  - Runs `UBehaviorTreeGraph::UpdateAsset`, saves, and reads the graph and
    Blackboard pointers back before success.
- `set_ai_behavior_tree_blackboard(behavior_tree_path, blackboard_path, ...)`
  - Synchronizes the runtime Behavior Tree pointer and the editor graph root,
    runs `UpdateBlackboardChange` plus `UpdateAsset`, saves, and verifies both
    readbacks.
- `search_ai_behavior_tree_node_classes(category="all", query="", ...)`
  - Searches loaded UE 5.6 composite, task, decorator, and service classes.
  - Native classes are complete for loaded AIModule types; Blueprint-generated
    classes appear when their class is loaded in the editor.
- `create_ai_eqs_query(asset_name, asset_root="/Game/AI/EQS", ...)`
  - Creates the same blank standard `UEnvQuery` object produced by the UE 5.6
    factory and saves it after readback.
  - EQS option/generator/test graph authoring is deliberately excluded from
    this minimal port.

All mutation tools are editor transactions, reject MCP-only references, refuse
to run during PIE/SIE, save by default, and return an explicit native readback.
Authored assets contain only engine/project types and remain usable with the
UnrealMCP plugin disabled. Existing Behavior Trees, Blackboards, linked key
types, and AIController Blueprints are checked for transitive package
dependencies before mutation and checked again before save. Read-only and
no-op responses use the same deep audit without dirtying the asset.

## Default Fixture

- Pawn asset: `/Game/Cubeless/Reactive/BP_Piper_ReactivePrototype`
- Skeletal mesh fallback: `/Game/Cubeless/Character/Piper/SK_Piper`
- Anim Blueprint fallback: `/Game/Cubeless/Character/Animation/ABP_RPGChracter`
- Actor label prefix: `MCP_AIDummySmoke`
- Behavior asset root: `/Game/Cubeless/AI/Smoke`
- Behavior Tree name: `BT_AIDummyPatrolChase`
- Blackboard name: `BB_AIDummyPatrolChase`

The smoke intentionally uses temporary actors in the current level and cleans
them up after SIE ends. It does not save a level or create project runtime code.

## Pass Criteria

- Patrol: the dummy reaches the patrol target within the configured pass
  distance.
- Detection: the player dummy is within `sight_radius` and
  `AIController.line_of_sight_to(player)` returns true.
- Chase: distance to the player decreases by the required delta after the chase
  command.
- Dependency audit: configured asset paths do not include MCP-only reference
  tokens such as `/Script/UnrealMCP`, `/UnrealMCP`, `UnrealMCP`,
  `MCPUnreal`, or `mcp_unreal`.
- BT/BB authoring: generated assets use standard `AIModule` classes and the
  C++ helper audits generated package objects for MCP-only tokens before
  returning success.
- Selector BT authoring: the chase branch has a standard Blackboard decorator
  for `TargetActor` with reactive aborts, so perception updates can interrupt
  patrol or retarget chase. The alert selector shape also verifies the
  face-target task and short wait before chase.
- AI Perception authoring: configured AIController Blueprints use standard
  `UAIPerceptionComponent` and `UAISenseConfig_Sight` objects only.
- BT execution: the saved Behavior Tree starts through
  `AIController.run_behavior_tree`, keeps Blackboard values set, and moves the
  dummy by the required delta in SIE.

## Notes

UE 5.6 exposes Behavior Tree and Blackboard asset factories to Unreal Python,
but not every stock Behavior Tree node class is directly exposed. The stable
path is therefore split:

- The C++ helper creates standard BT/BB assets and audits their package objects.
- The SIE smoke validates engine AI movement and line-of-sight behavior without
  saving level content.
- The BT execution smoke validates the saved Behavior Tree runtime path without
  introducing project runtime code.

This helper does not introduce runtime gameplay classes, components, or
UnrealMCP references into generated content.
